<title>SINGAPORE: Liang Huat slips into red at half-time.</title>
<headline>Liang Huat slips into red at half-time.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   (loss)  0.62  vs   2.29  (gain)</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)	  (loss)  0.28  vs   1.05  (gain)</p>
<p>    Turnover				48.35  vs  44.97</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.71  vs   0.33</p>
<p>    Interest expense		     1.02  vs   0.26</p>
<p>    Depreciation			   1.45  vs   0.73</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     (loss)  0.07  vs   3.39  (gain)</p>
<p>    Tax					0.84  vs   1.09</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (gain)  0.29  vs    -</p>
<p>Note - Liang Huat Aluminium Ltd said its construction division suffered a loss due to a competitive market and increasing costs.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703180) sd ds</p>
</text>
